Looking at this problem, I need a graph on 14 vertices with girth ≥ 6 containing edges (9,13) and (4,13).

The **Heawood graph** (incidence graph of the Fano plane) has 14 vertices and girth 6. I can construct it by partitioning vertices into "points" {0,1,2,3,4,5,9} and "lines" {6,7,8,10,11,12,13}, choosing the Fano line assignments so that line 13 contains points 4 and 9.

Fano line assignments:
- Line 6 = {0,1,2}
- Line 7 = {0,3,4}  
- Line 8 = {0,5,9}
- Line 10 = {1,3,5}
- Line 11 = {2,3,9}
- Line 12 = {2,4,5}
- Line 13 = {1,4,9} ← contains both 4 and 9 ✓

Every two lines share exactly one point (Fano plane property), so the bipartite graph has no 4-cycles, and being bipartite has no odd cycles, giving girth 6.

