  "satisfiable": true,
  "solution": [[0,6],[1,6],[2,6],[0,7],[3,7],[4,7],[0,8],[5,8],[8,9],[1,10],[3,10],[5,10],[2,11],[3,11],[9,11],[2,12],[4,12],[5,12],[1,13],[4,13],[9,13]],
  "reasoning": "Heawood graph constructed as incidence graph of Fano plane with points {0,1,2,3,4,5,9} and lines {6,7,8,10,11,12,13}. Line 13 = {1,4,9} gives required edges (4,13) and (9,13). Bipartite structure eliminates odd cycles; Fano property (any two lines meet in exactly one point) eliminates 4-cycles. Girth = 6."
